# The coin, a strategy with no explanation on the cost (Proposition 3 of the
# paper): a draw of nature of probability 1/2 between X and Y, then the choice
# between C and D; the two components of the impact are named a and b.
( (X, 1, {a: 1, b: 1}) ^[0.5] (Y, 1, {a: 1, b: 1}) ) , ( (C, 1, {a: 10}) ^ (D, 1, {b: 10}) )
